#{[17592186542102 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542102 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9aca599-1b05-506b-80c8-6fbc19e4fd06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1069 "q-46396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the inverse of $f(x)=5-9{x}^{2}$ for $x\\ge 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0439240f-2359-52c3-a019-0d15653653ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542111 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=5-9{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=5-9{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5-9{y}^{2} \\\\ x-5 & =-9{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{5-x}{9} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5-x}{9}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1069 "q-46395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the inverse of $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-6$ for $x\\ge 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "10ace3a5-6164-50ba-ba18-c598288b7099" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542117 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=2{x}^{2}-6\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=2{y}^{2}-6\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ x+6 & =2{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+6}{2} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x+6}{2}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222071" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-10{x}^{2}+40x-27$ for $x\\le 2.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1749af1b-7a2a-52a7-adf9-0527962ea5b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542121 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-10{x}^{2}+40x-27 \\\\  & =-10({x}^{2}-4x)-27 \\\\  & =-10(({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2})-27 \\\\  & =-10((x-2)^{2}-4)-27 \\\\  & =-10{(x-2)}^{2}+40-27 \\\\  & =-10{(x-2)}^{2}+13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-10{(x-2)}^{2}+13\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=-10{(y-2)}^{2}+13\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-10{(y-2)}^{2}+13 \\\\ 10{(y-2)}^{2} & =13-x \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{13-x}{10} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}} \\\\ y & =2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the negative square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\le 2,$ then the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is  ${f}^{-1}\\le 2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{13-x}{10}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143084" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4x+7$ for $x\\ge 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2079d901-07f2-590c-b43f-09625015f43f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542126 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =2{x}^{2}-4x+7 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-2x)+7 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2})+7 \\\\  & =2((x-1)^{2}-1)+7 \\\\  & =2(x-1)^{2}-2+7 \\\\  & =2(x-1)^{2}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=2(x-1)^{2}+5\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=2(y-1)^{2}+5\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2(y-1)^{2}+5 \\\\ x-5 & =2(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x-5}{2} & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}} & =y-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{2}}+1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-40x+15$ for $x\\ge 5.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79783b94-bb53-5240-8c0c-52c93a581d6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542162 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =4{x}^{2}-40x+15 \\\\  & =4({x}^{2}-10x)+15 \\\\  & =4({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =4((x-5)^{2}-25)+15 \\\\  & =4(x-5)^{2}-100+15 \\\\  & =4(x-5)^{2}-85\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=4(x-5)^{2}-85\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=4(y-5)^{2}-85\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4(y-5)^{2}-85 \\\\ x+85 & =4(y-5)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+85}{4} & =(y-5)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{x+85}{4}} & =y-5 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 5$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 5.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+85}}{2}+5\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-46409" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+2x+5$ for $x\\ge 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87d49f48-029f-525c-b4c7-c630bf956527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542163 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{2}+2x+5 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2x)+5 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2})+5 \\\\  & =-((x-1)^{2}-1)+5 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+1+5 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-(x-1)^{2}+6\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-(y-1)^{2}+6\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y-1)^{2}+6 \\\\ x-6 & =-(y-1)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{-x+6} & =y-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{-x+6}+1 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 1$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 1.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{-x+6}+1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143069" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the inverse of $f(x)=8-3{x}^{2}$ for $x\\ge 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ea93b33-07b4-5d80-ad03-66a9bad29401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542167 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=8-3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=8-3{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8-3{y}^{2} \\\\ x-8 & =-3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{8-x}{3} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{8-x}{3}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143057" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-12x+13$ for $x\\le 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5d4ec46-41de-5071-92d0-61a853c21e80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542194 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3{x}^{2}-12x+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-4x)+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x)+13 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+13 \\\\  & =3((x-2)^{2}-4)+13 \\\\  & =3(x-2)^{2}-12+13 \\\\  & =3(x-2)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=3(x-2)^{2}+1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=3(y-2)^{2}+1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3(y-2)^{2}+1 \\\\ 3(y-2)^{2} & =x-1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{x-1}{3} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}} \\\\ y & =2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the negative square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\le 2,$ then the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is  ${f}^{-1}\\le 2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-12x+40$ for $x\\ge 6.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b957784b-0ac4-5ba4-bc18-3ca9998ce9ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542199 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}-12x+40 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})-{6}^{2}+40 \\\\  & =(x-6)^{2}-36+40 \\\\  & =(x-6)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x-6)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y-6)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y-6)^{2}+4 \\\\ x-4 & =(y-6)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4} & =y-6 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4}+6 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 6$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 6.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-4}+6\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=1-4{x}^{2}$ for $x\\le 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d281164a-5064-5f5c-ac1f-851a58f31d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542211 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=1-4{x}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=1-4{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1-4{y}^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =-4{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1-x}{4} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x\\le 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\le 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-x}{4}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+4x-4$ for $x\\ge -2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eaa3b305-adcb-5660-ac47-ef5d46e7e553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542218 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}+4x-4 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-4-4 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x+2)^{2}-8\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y+2)^{2}-8\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y+2)^{2}-8 \\\\ x+8 & =(y+2)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x+8} & =y+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+8}-2 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge -2$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge -2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x+8}-2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{2}-1$ for $x\\le 0.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "effbd8f4-b559-5948-841a-8a16bd6f2c1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542224 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-3{x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=-3{y}^{2}-1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ x+1 & =-3{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{x+1}{3} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{-\\frac{x+1}{3}} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if $x\\le 0$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\le 0.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\sqrt{-\\frac{x+1}{3}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
